# The Nvidia GPU architectures both backends are built for, one per line,
# oldest first. Numbers only: 86 means compute_86 and sm_86.
#
# Read by configure.ac for libavian_cuda.so and by
# scripts/windows/build-cuda-dll.ps1 for avian_cuda.dll, so the two platforms
# cover the same hardware. Edit here, not in either. Anything the installed
# toolkit cannot emit is dropped, and PTX is emitted for the newest one that
# survives, so a card released after the build still runs by driver JIT.
#
# PTX only works forwards. A build whose oldest cubin is sm_86 does not run
# on anything older, whatever PTX it carries, so the list is the whole of the
# backward compatibility story.

# Maxwell and Pascal, a 900 or 10 series card. They cost about five minutes
# of build and seven megabytes, measured, and the X16RT tuning tables
# upstream are full of 1060s and 1080s, so they stay while any toolkit still
# offers them.
52
61
# Turing, the 16 and 20 series.
75
# Ampere: 80 is the A100, 86 the 30 series.
80
86
# Ada, the 40 series.
89
# Blackwell: 100 is the datacentre part, 120 the 50 series.
100
120
